The main saving is calling `GetType()` once and reusing the result. It is a virtual call, and the original makes it twice on the non-string path. This assumes `GetType()` is a side-effect-free getter, as it is in the SDK. All return values are unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 FieldBase::GetNumValues(void) const
{
    if (!IsValid())
        return 0;

    const FIT_UINT8 type = GetType();

    if (type == FIT_BASE_TYPE_STRING)
        return (FIT_UINT8)stringIndexes.size();

    return (FIT_UINT8)(values.size() / baseTypeSizes[type & FIT_BASE_TYPE_NUM_MASK]);
}
```